hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22878","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us: Huraym ibn Sufyan narrated to us, from Bayan, from Qays, from Abu Shahm, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A slave girl passed by me in Medina, so I took her by her side. He said: And in the morning the Messenger, pledging the people, meaning the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came. He said: So I came to him and he did not pledge me. So he said: The one of the little locust, now. He said: I said: By Allah, I will not return. He said: So he pledged me."
"22879","Surayj narrated to us: Yazid ibn Ata narrated to us, from Bayan ibn Bishr, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Abu Shahm, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I was an idle man. He said: So a slave girl passed by me on one of the roads of Medina, when I reached for her side. So when morning came, he said: So the people came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pledging him, so I came to him and stretched my hand to pledge him, so he withheld his hand and said: I think you are the one of the little locust, meaning: Are you not the one of the little locust yesterday? He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, pledge me, for by Allah, I will not return ever. He said: So yes, then."
